    "rungPopulationsNote": "Contract for the inc1 loader/interpolator (Bev, 2026-09-09): the expected rung count and exact population sequence a consumer validates rungs[].population against. Every numeric leaf on a rung, at any nesting depth including array elements, is finite and non-negative and is the interpolation target (log-linear in population per traffic-assumptions.md A-6); every non-numeric leaf (densityBand, provenance) carries through verbatim from the lower bracketing rung rather than being interpolated. BUG-823 rule: every field under a rung's provenance subtree (including year) is a STRING by rule, never a numeric leaf — provenance is entirely non-numeric so it is never mistaken for an interpolation target (a numeric year would otherwise interpolate to a fractional year, e.g. 2026.4).",
    "comment2": "THE scale-ladder LUT (table k). One row per population rung, ascending. Runtime consumers interpolate log-linearly between rows (see traffic-assumptions.md A-6); never extrapolate beyond the last rung (98,000,000)."
